               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>12ã€What parameters and sensors does             vLinker MC supp</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>12ã€What parameters and sensors does             vLinker MC support for OBDII?</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>The vLinker MC supports the standard OBDII parameters (PIDs)  a</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>The vLinker MC supports the standard OBDII parameters (PIDs)  as defined in SAE J1979 AUG2014(OBD AUTO DOCTOR app) .</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>The actual list of available parameters is vehicle specific. Yo</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>The actual list of available parameters is vehicle specific. Your  vehicle must have those sensors to work with app.Different  OBDII app might support different list of parameters and sensors.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Please refer to : https://www.obdautodoctor.com/obd-parameters</photoshop:LayerName>
